			<div class="content" id="post-content-1912086">
									

<p>Sorry I did not see your comments before!</p>
<p>When I first had this idea I wasn’t sure what to do with it. I was wondering about making it a funny piece, or maybe a –J. I knew it could not work just on itself and it needed some kind of story, so I decided to go for something more dramatic.</p>
<p>I decided to make a parallel with the high number of murdered or disappeared aboriginal woman in the more remote locations. If someone gets murdered and nobody else cares, it's like a tree falling and not making a sound. So the guy is convinced his girlfriend has been murdered and is tormented by not knowing what happened exactly, and by how little people care.</p>
<p>The letter is trying to hint that the anomalous properties developed following something the guy did. Possibly communicate with the trees of the forest to find out what happened to his girlfriend (guided by a friend who has a ''special'' knowledge of plants). His present condition could be due to an adverse side-effect, or possibly some form of price he paid for the knowledge. Even he doesn’t know anymore.</p>

							</div>

								
